{
  "slug": "clinic-treatment-fit",
  "title": "Treatment suitability check",
  "category": "Clinics",
  "summary": "Screens out enquiries a clinic cannot treat, then scores suitability and commitment. Written to keep clinical claims out of the funnel.",
  "shape": "GATED_ASSESSMENT",
  "aiInstructions": "You are writing the note a clinic coordinator reads before calling an enquiry back.\n\nWrite 200 to 280 words, addressed to the person in second person, calm and factual. Reflect what their answers say about their expectations, their preparation and their circumstances, using the category names as evidence.\n\nABSOLUTE LIMITS. Never diagnose. Never name a condition. Never state or imply that any treatment is suitable, unsuitable, safe or effective for them. Never give a timeline, a price or an outcome. Never advise them to start, stop or change any medication or treatment.\n\nWhat you MAY do is describe what a consultation will need to establish, and what they can usefully prepare. End by saying that only a qualified clinician who has examined them can answer the clinical questions.",
